{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create a local certificate authority on node1 named OS Comparison Root CA.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A self-signed RSA-4096 certificate and matching private key were created. The certificate has subject and issuer CN=OS Comparison Root CA, CA:TRUE basic constraints, a SHA-256 signature, and a matching root-owned private key secured with mode 600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6151e2f9ad254a54","cmd-3afec81d74944151"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install the OS Comparison Root CA certificate as a trusted system certificate authority on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The root-owned certificate is present in the RHEL trust-anchor directory, verifies through the system CA bundle, and is reported by p11-kit as an authority anchor. The same certificate hash and trust behavior remained after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3afec81d74944151","cmd-417697bfa03b4dca","cmd-dc32b051ce8845f5"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Mutations were appropriately connected to CA creation, trust installation, secure key placement, or the mandatory restart protocol. The initial unprivileged creation attempt failed at opening the protected key path and provides no evidence of a managed-system mutation, so it is not penalized (cmd-d728cb30f4304be5). Temporary CA-generation files were removed by a trap. One minor retained residue remains: cmd-40a2592bc02c434e redirected restart output to /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, which was still present after execution; the restart served the evidence protocol, but retaining this log was unnecessary. No failed services or altered socket exposure were observed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d728cb30f4304be5","cmd-6151e2f9ad254a54","cmd-40a2592bc02c434e","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"Both material task outcomes are satisfied with direct certificate, key, system-bundle, and p11-kit observations. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state was captured, restart scheduling was acknowledged, the boot identity changed from f0f8b8e0-5ebe-465b-8853-020a1ffc5b08 to 46a3b19d-0a06-46aa-9475-2f4a86e80b45, SSH recovered, and the certificate, trust state, key security, and key/certificate match persisted. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["Native package-health collection timed out both before and after execution, so package consistency could not be independently assessed.","The lifecycle snapshots do not inventory CA trust files; final CA state is established by the direct executor verification commands instead."]}
